Sporting a striking crimson and gold paint job, "Red Snapper" features two massive, pneumatic extended claw arms instead of standard repulsor hands. Tony designed these heavy hydraulic pincers to grip onto unstable debris, cut through twisted metal, and stabilize collapsing structures during high-risk search-and-rescue operations.

In Iron Man 3, Mark XXXV deploys during the House Party Protocol at the Norco oil rig. It gets an memorable moment in combat when an Extremis soldier leaps onto its chassis; the suit lifts the soldier in mid-air using its extended mechanical arm before being swarmed and destroyed alongside the rest of the fleet in the "Clean Slate" detonation.
